#: inc/admin-screen.php:309
msgid "If you find this plugin useful, the most valuable thing you can do for us is mention us to a nonprofit who might benefit from our services. Referrals are how our business continues to grow its impact and reach."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:315
msgid "Learn about Groundwork Common"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:325
msgid "You can also support our WordPress plugins directly. While we offer the plugin free to you, it costs us to maintain it — the security updates, the compatibility testing against each new WordPress release, the bug nobody but you has hit. We can’t do it without your support, and we appreciate whatever support you can give."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:330
msgid "Support our work"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:337
msgid "Report a problem"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:366
msgid "Results shown at once"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:367
msgid "0 shows every match. Any other number shows that many with a “Show all results” button after them. This limits what is drawn, never what is searched — a location beyond the cut is still found by typing its name."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:373
msgid "Offer sorting by distance"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:374
msgid "Lets a visitor share their location to sort the results by how near they are. Off removes it entirely."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:380
msgid "Ask before loading the map"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:381
msgid "Show a placeholder with a \"Show map\" button instead of loading map tiles straight away. Tiles are fetched by the visitor's browser, so until they choose to load them their IP address is never sent to the tile provider. The search, filters and location list all work without the map. Has no effect when the tiles are served from this site, since there is no third party involved."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:387
msgid "Ask for location on arrival"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:388
msgid "Off by default, deliberately: an unprompted permission prompt is easy to refuse and hard to ask for twice, and browsers penalize sites that do it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:395
msgid "Distance units"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:396
msgid "Left automatic, this follows the site language — miles for US and UK English, kilometers everywhere else."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:404
msgid "Timezone for “Open now”"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:405
msgid "the site timezone"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:406
msgid "An IANA name such as America/Chicago. Left blank this follows Settings → General, which is almost always right: somebody checking a Birmingham food bank from a phone still set to Pacific time wants Birmingham’s clock."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:414
msgid "Zoom to fit the results"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:415
msgid "On, the map frames whatever is currently showing. The starting point below is the fallback for when nothing matches, so it is worth setting even with this on."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:423
msgid "Starting latitude"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:424
msgid "Defaults to 0, which is a point in the Gulf of Guinea — fine while results are showing, and an ocean the moment a filter matches nothing."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:432
msgid "Starting longitude"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:441
msgid "Starting zoom"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:442
msgid "0 is the whole world, 12 a city, 16 a few streets."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:451
msgid "Directions service"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:452
msgid "Where the Directions link sends people. The address is used in preference to the coordinates, because a street address resolves to a door and a coordinate resolves to a point — which on a large site is regularly the wrong side of the building."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:458
msgid "Custom directions URL"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:460
msgid "Only used when the service above is Custom. {query} is the formatted address, {lat} and {lng} the coordinates."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:468
msgid "Contact address for lookups"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:479
msgid "Sent with each lookup so the address service knows which site is asking. Leave it blank to use your admin email. Without a contact address the service can refuse the request, and the address finder in the location editor stops filling in coordinates."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:485
msgid "Lookup endpoint"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:487
msgid "Point this at your own Nominatim instance, or a paid provider with a compatible response."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:493
msgid "Limit lookups to countries"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:495
msgid "Two-letter codes, comma separated. Leave blank to search everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:501
msgid "Prefer results in this box"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:503
msgid "Four numbers: west, south, east, north. Nudges results toward your region without excluding the rest."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:509
msgid "Restrict strictly to that box"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:510
msgid "Turns the preference above into a hard limit. An address outside the box then returns nothing at all, which looks like a broken lookup rather than a deliberate one — leave this off unless you mean it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:518
msgid "Tile URL"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:520
msgid "Only used when Map style on the Appearance tab is set to Custom. Must contain {z}, {x} and {y}."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:526
msgid "Tile attribution"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:527
msgid "Printed on the map. Nearly every tile provider requires this, and removing it breaks their terms rather than merely being impolite. Links are allowed."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:535
msgid "Deepest zoom offered"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:536
msgid "Zooming past what a provider actually has produces blank tiles."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:550
msgid "Which field drives what"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:551
msgid "A location can carry more than one address, schedule or closure list — a mailing address and a visiting one, pantry hours and office hours. They all display; these choose which of them the finder acts on."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:554
msgid "Results"
